ow how to  manage that patient so when they were  always asked for medical advice i said  never give medical advice unless you're  going to go with a physician and see the  patient  so  that's sort of a modification of  this  i don't feel comfortable answering that  question  yeah absolutely um thank you so much  again dr murray i think i think that's  all the questions we're going to have  time for today we really appreciate all  your attendance and your involvement in  the q a  and we look forward to any follow-up  questions we might receive and and thank  you again for attending this  presentation will be available on demand  demand after this live session is  complete and you will receive a link to  that in the email you provided  so thank you again everyone and feel  free to forward that link to anyone who  may have missed today's live event  until next time  uh we hope we see oh yeah yeah jordan i  like to also thank everybody i enjoyed  the opportunity i sort of missed this i  did it for so many years  um i hope that what we presented was was  useful  um i always would sort of in my  presentations by challenging the  audience  to take what they learned today  and make one change do one thing  different than what they were doing  yesterday that's going to improve what  you do whether it's what you do in the  laboratory what you do in the  pre-analytical site what you do and  managing patients but take something  from this instead of just absorbing the  knowledge  and apply it to a patient and help that  patient and i think if you do that then  we've been successful in this  presentation so again thank you to the  audience  thank you so much everyone thanks  you

